# Cairn mobile — environment variables
#
# Copy to `.env.local` (gitignored) and fill in. Values are read at build time
# by Expo. `.env.local` is NEVER committed.
#
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Apple code signing (native, build-time only — NOT bundled into the app)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Your Apple Developer team ID. Used by plugins/withAppleSigning.js to enable
# automatic on-device code signing during `expo prebuild`. If unset, the plugin
# is skipped (Xcode manual signing still works). Find it at:
# https://developer.apple.com/account → Membership → Team ID.
APPLE_TEAM_ID=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# AI backend
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Cairn's chat + note AI actions run through a pluggable provider:
#
#   1. Rork toolkit  — first-party only. Set EXPO_PUBLIC_TOOLKIT_URL to the Rork
#                      base URL at build time. It is INTENTIONALLY left blank
#                      here and must NEVER be committed: the Rork endpoint is
#                      unauthenticated, so a leaked URL lets anyone run up our
#                      server bill. Keep the real value in .env.local only.
#
#   2. OpenAI-compatible — the default for anyone building Cairn themselves.
#                      Leave EXPO_PUBLIC_TOOLKIT_URL blank and configure a base
#                      URL + API key in the app (Settings → AI). No env var
#                      needed; the key is stored in the device keychain.
#
# If EXPO_PUBLIC_TOOLKIT_URL is set, the app uses Rork. Otherwise it uses the
# in-app OpenAI-compatible configuration.
#
# NOTE: EXPO_PUBLIC_* vars are inlined into the shipped JS bundle, so this value
# is extractable from a built app. Env only keeps it out of git/source.
EXPO_PUBLIC_TOOLKIT_URL=
